---
// Import the CSS file from the same directory
import '../styling/style.css';
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout title="Home">
	<div class="main">
		<header>
			<h1>Hey, I'm Tiam!</h1>
			<h3 class="hero-subtitle">High school student, all-around nerd.</h3>
		</header>

		<section>
			<h2 class="sub-heading">About me</h2>
			<div class="intro-text">
				<p>
					Quick intro: Hi, my name is <b>Tiam Hadjian</b> and I'm 15 years old.
					I've lived in <b>Germany</b> with my parents and little brother all my life, 
					but I'm 99% sure I'm 100% <b>Persian</b> or <b>Iranian</b>, or whatever you 
					want to call it. <i>There's all my personal information, you creep.</i>
				</p>

				<p>
					I've played the <b>piano</b> since I was 8, and I love <b>coding</b> in my free time.
					I also sometimes play around in <b>Blender</b>, which—fun fact—is the only software
					where beginners manage to confuse the pros <i>(I don't know what I'm doing)</i>.
				</p>

				<p>
					I'm also part of my school's robotics team, <a href="https://github.com/Bento-Robotics" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"><b>Bento Robotics</b></a> <i>(sponsors are appreciated)</i>, where we compete in the RMRC (Rapidly Manufactured Robot Challenge) 
					at the <b>RoboCup</b> <i>(not to brag, but we won the <b>German Open</b> competition and came 8th at the World Championships)</i>. 
					We're also open-source, so if you were wondering: yes, you can steal our code.
				</p>

				<p>
					I've also recently picked up photography as a hobby after I found my dad's <b>Canon 1200D</b> 
					<i>(or Rebel T5 for all my freedom people)</i>. I'll link my Instagram here if I ever get around 
					to making one <i>(I probably won't)</i>.
				</p>

				<p>
					Anyway, enough about me and more about me. This website is dedicated to all of my 
					<b>coding projects</b> and maybe some random <b>blogs</b> on the side. All of these projects were
					made for fun in my free time, so there's a not so small chance that you might find some
					absolutely <b>horrendous</b> sights, like a swarm of nested <code>if</code> statements.
				</p>

				<p>
					But that's not what this page is about. It's not about the <b>prettiest</b> code or the 
					most <b>efficient</b> algorithms. I made this page to showcase and document my somewhat questionable learning 
					progress, so that I can look back and laugh in 10 years' time.
				</p>

				<p class="ps-note">
					<i>P.S. Some of these projects are years old, but I only recently published them all to GitHub and created this website.</i>
				</p>
			</div>

			<footer class="site-credit">
				<p>(Heavily inspired by <a href="https://www.taniarascia.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Tania Rascia's</a> website)</p>
			</footer>
		</section>
	</div>
</BaseLayout>
